  "notes": "Blue-eyed-soul soloist in the Tim & Bob and Babyface orbit, 1995–2004. The research gives \"61–105 straight; ballads 61–77 half-time\", and the ballad band is the base — four of the five sourced tempos sit in it — with `halfTime` true and a `halftime_3` snare. Three drum deltas: \"soft-attack kit, kick on 1\" at one or two hits a bar with syncopation at 0.08, \"clap+snare on 3\" as a stack with a wider offset than the Tim & Bob norm, and \"16th hats in the chorus only\" at 0.14 fill density with the open hat pinned to `2&` rather than `4&`. The identifying parameter is harmonic and the research states it as a superlative: \"the most extension-heavy harmony in the male-soloist group — m9, maj9, sus2, 4-chord cycles rather than 2-chord vamps\". So the triad share is 0.08 — the lowest in the section — ninth matches seventh at 0.46, `susSubstitutionProb` is 0.4 for the sus2 colour, and every family is four chords deep. \"Falsetto stacks\" and the guitar counterline give the high melody ceiling and a counter at −12. The bass is \"electric-bass-style synth on roots and 5ths, slides between chord tones\", so the cells are root-fifth-octave and `glideProb` is 0.28, with no `bass808` block. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks its key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity, density and register number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode with jazz extensions [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
